"Every Claude has to be closed first, this profile's and every other one. An instance builds its sidebar as it starts and rewrites records in its own shape as it runs, so chats copied underneath a running one are invisible at best and written over at worst.\n\nCopying leaves the originals where they are, so the other profile is unchanged and still has them if that account is ever signed back into over there. Nothing already here is written over either, so a chat this profile has archived or renamed keeps the shape it was given.\n\nOnly the small record files are copied; the messages themselves already live in ~/.claude and are shared either way." = "Every Claude has to be closed first, this profile's and every other one. An instance builds its sidebar as it starts and rewrites records in its own shape as it runs, so chats copied underneath a running one are invisible at best and written over at worst.\n\nCopying leaves the originals where they are, so the other profile is unchanged and still has them if that account is ever signed back into over there. Nothing already here is written over either, so a chat this profile has archived or renamed keeps the shape it was given.\n\nOnly the small record files are copied; the messages themselves already live in ~/.claude and are shared either way.";

